diff --git a/packages/should-skip-package/README.md b/packages/should-skip-package/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3c817c3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packages/should-skip-package/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+# @changesets/should-skip-package
+
+Use `shouldSkipPackageReason(pkg, options)` to learn why a package is skipped. It returns:
+
+- `"ignored"` when the package name appears in `options.ignore`;
+- `"private"` when the package is private and `options.allowPrivatePackages` is `false`;
+- `"missing-version"` when the package has no version; or
+- `null` when the package should not be skipped.
+
+Checks use that precedence: ignored, then disallowed private, then missing version. An allowed private package can therefore still return `"missing-version"`.
+
+`shouldSkipPackage(pkg, options)` remains the boolean compatibility API. It returns `true` exactly when `shouldSkipPackageReason(pkg, options)` is not `null`.
diff --git a/packages/should-skip-package/src/index.test.ts b/packages/should-skip-package/src/index.test.ts
